  You ain't just whistlin' Dixie brother!
  I was the first one to complain about this on the Unix system.  I was 
finally able to narrow the problem down to one line of code:

       while(resists_ston(&mons[otmp->corpsenm])) {

  This appears on line 796 of mklev.c.  The system does not like this par-
ticular line of code.  What is even stranger is that there is an EXACT copy
of this line later in the same program (the game only crashes when the above
line is left in the program).  I don't know why it crashes.  My solution was
to comment out the small section of code that contained this line (as far as
I know this area dealt with statues on the Medusa level).  It worked.  I 
would, however, like to know WHY it crashes with this line included.
  Any ideas?
 
